THERE-IS-NO-PYOCD-TARGET-FOR-THIS-PART
# `python -m pyocd list --targets | grep -i xmc` matches nothing in pyocd
# 0.45.1, the version installed here, and nothing in its built-in table
# starts with xmc. `pyocd pack install` cannot help either, because that
# fetches a support pack for a target name that already resolves.
#
# So tools/capture.py cannot flash or reset this part. The line above is a
# sentinel rather than a name: pyocd will reject it and say so, which is
# the intended failure - better than an empty file that reads as "not
# filled in yet" or a plausible-looking name that resolves to some other
# die.
#
# The research tree hit the same wall and programs this part through
# J-Link with pylink instead, recording that in its board registry rather
# than leaving the next session to rediscover it. Doing the same here
# means a J-Link path in tools/, which this port did not add.
